# gtk2 — built FROM SOURCE via a novadeck-owned PKGBUILD (packages/gtk2/PKGBUILD), NOT fetched
# from the holo monorepo: holo has NO gtk2 to fetch a PKGBUILD for (SteamOS ships none). This is
# the "local PKGBUILD" form (like packages/mesa/source.pin); makepkg still clones the upstream
# GNOME git tag named in the PKGBUILD.
#
# Why: the native arm64 Steam client's steamui.so links libgtk-x11-2.0.so.0. We now ship gtk2 on
# the HOST (it's in customize-base.sh PKGS, installed from this overlay ahead of holo) instead of
# resolving it from Steam's bundled SR3 runtime via pressure-vessel. See packages/README.md for
# the overlay mechanism and the holo-pacman-no-gtk2 note.
#
# Fields:
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); also the work/ build-dir + repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path (relative to this dir) to the checked-in PKGBUILD to build
#   pkgrel_suffix  numeric suffix appended to the PKGBUILD's pkgrel (N -> N.<suffix>) so pacman
#                  prefers our build on later upgrades. Integer only (makepkg requires
#                  pkgrel = integer[.integer]).
#   patches        space-separated files under ./patches/, applied `patch -p1` in the gtk source
#                  root (after `cd gtk` in prepare()), in the order listed. These are the upstream
#                  Arch patches (XID-warning severity; CVE-2024-6655 stop-loading-modules-from-cwd).
#
# To bump gtk2: edit pkgver in packages/gtk2/PKGBUILD, re-verify both patches apply against the new
# tag (patch -p1 --dry-run on a shallow clone), and re-roll any patch whose hunk fails.
name: gtk2
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
patches: 0001-Lower-severity-of-XID-collision-warnings.patch 0002-Stop-looking-for-modules-in-cwd.patch
